    "scriptCode": "// --- LISSAJOUS LAYERS ---\n// Lissajous figures, one above the other: the same frequencies A and B,\n// with the phase advancing from layer to layer over half a turn, so the\n// stack shows how the figure changes with the phase. The phase also\n// runs with the time t: the figures turn into one another, layer by layer.\n// The Meshes field sets how many layers; the stack keeps its height.\nA := int(1,9);\nB := int(1,9);\n//MESH_BEGIN\nu: 0, TAU, 200\nv: 0, TAU, 32\n//MESH_END\nfloat phase = mesh * 3.14159265 / meshes + 0.5*t;\nfloat z = (mesh - 0.5 * (meshes - 1.0)) * 1.8 / max(meshes - 1.0, 1.0);\nreturn vec4(sin(A*u + phase), sin(B*u), z, 0.0);\n",
